How attribution is carried
--------------------------
Neither CrossInk nor biscuit puts a copyright header on individual source
files, so there is no upstream header to preserve — saying otherwise would
describe a practice that cannot be followed. Instead:

  • Every ported file carries a short provenance comment naming its source
    project, its licence, and its copyright holder.
  • Every ported app directory carries a PORT_NOTES.md recording what the
    original did, what the merge gate changed, and why.
  • The MIT copyright notice and permission text required by the licence are
    carried in LICENSE.merge, distributed with the firmware.

Both CrossInk and biscuit are MIT and share the same copyright holder, so
nothing here requires relicensing. See LICENSE.merge for the full terms.
